% Discounts by customer tier (LPS2's rule base, as valid DRL; a decision service) (the decision-service reading)
%
% The timeless Logical English twin of a Drools rule base that only inserts facts (a decision
% service), written by the DRL translator (InsurLE2/migration/drools) from discount.drl: each inserted
% type is concluded by rules; rules concluding one type are an otherwise cascade in salience order.

the target language is: prolog.

the templates are:
    there is a customer called *a name* with tier *a tier*.
    there is an order for *a customer* with size *a size*.
    there is a discount for *a customer* with rate *a rate*.

the knowledge base discount includes:

the text of the rule base is at "sources/discount.drl".

% The rules concluding this, in salience order (the first that applies wins): an otherwise cascade of
%   - "Gold customers with a large order get the best rate" (salience 10)
%   - "Everyone else with a large order gets the standard rate" (salience 5)
there is a discount for a customer with rate a rate if
    there is an order for the customer with size large
    and all of
        there is a customer called the customer with tier gold
        and the rate is equal to best
        otherwise it is not the case that there is a customer called the customer with tier gold
        and the rate is equal to standard.

scenario drools_run is, as stated in the Drools run:
    there is an order for acme with size large.
    there is a customer called acme with tier gold.
    there is an order for zeta with size large.
    there is a customer called zeta with tier silver.
    there is an order for tiny with size small.
    discount expects answers ["there is a discount for acme with rate best", "there is a discount for zeta with rate standard"].

query discount is:
    there is a discount for which customer with rate which rate.

